#
# What raft/zhen_app.py imports at run time, and nothing else: the input of
# raft/runtime/requirements.txt, the hash-locked list the unit's venv is built
# from (deploy/systemd/unheaded-zhen-app.service, S-ZHEN-FRONT D-05).
#
#   scripts/ci-python-lock.sh raft/runtime
#   pip install --require-hashes --no-deps --only-binary=:all: -r raft/runtime/requirements.txt
#
# Every version is the one ~/.venv/zhen runs today. No package is new: each
# name is already in the dependency baseline (ADR-096). Not here, on purpose:
# the training and eval packages of raft/requirements.txt (datasets, peft, trl,
# anthropic, faiss-cpu, langchain-text-splitters) and pytest. The app imports
# none of them.
#
# torch is PyPI's Linux build, the one that runs today. A CPU-only wheel comes
# from another index, which is a new source and Stevie's decision.

# --- web + API surface -------------------------------------------------------
